    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a challenging slate today, with several bats navigating the dangerous arm of Corbin Burns. Despite the tough matchup, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (58.63) and **Kyle Tucker** (66.99) emerge as our primary anchors. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a high-floor matchup against Landen Roupp, whose 4.07 xERA provides the most favorable pitcher profile on the board. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** earns his high ranking despite facing Burns; his score is buoyed by a significant 14% dynamic platoon boost and favorable wind conditions that help offset the elite opposing SP skill. **Andy Pages** (57.86) also remains a strong play in the OF4 slot, though we are tracking his lineup status closely as he projects to hit cleanup, providing critical RBI opportunities despite a minor penalty for facing a high-end catcher\u2019s pop time.\n\nOur middle-infield depth remains a volatile area, with **Nasim Nunez** (44.16) and **Brady House** (47.12) both fighting through the 3.01 xERA of Burns. While **Nasim Nunez** carries a lower raw floor, the favorable wind at his back provides enough of a situational nudge to keep him in the lineup over bench options. The most difficult decision today was the UTIL slot, where **Heliot Ramos** (42.73) barely edged out the rest of the bench. **Heliot Ramos** is squeezed by Emmet Sheehan\u2019s 3.16 xERA and a negative platoon adjustment, yet he retains the spot due to the high probability of hitting third in the order, which maximizes his exposure to run-scoring chances. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while rotation regulars **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill** are unavailable due to off-days, leaving our bench thin as we manage our game caps.",
